  "name": "Jehoshaphat",
  "title": "The God-fearing King of Judah",
  "era": "divided-kingdom",
  "lifespan": "c. 914–869 BC",
  "summary": "Jehoshaphat was the fourth king of Judah after the kingdom split. He was known for his godliness, his legal reforms, and his zeal to teach the people the law of the Lord. Despite some unfortunate alliances with the wicked kings of Israel, his reign is considered one of the most successful in Judah's history.",
